            <ArticleTitle>Proximal &quot;tube&quot; realignment of the patella for chondromalacia patellae.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>63-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In young people complaining of patellar pain there is often an anatomic basis (an increased quadriceps angle or a high-riding patella). Forty-eight knees with one or other of these abnormalities underwent proximal quadriceps realignment. The results were excellent or good in 94%. Shaving of chondromalacic cartilage was also done in 11 knees but did not seem to improve the results, and is not now recommended except for &quot;blister&quot; lesions. Extensor mechanism dysplasia is an etiologically correct name for the disorder and therefore preferable to &quot;chondromalacia patellae.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
